.SH NAME
toast_stack \- Stacked notifications: any number of toasts shown at once, in one column at the position of the first ([toasts] position by default), toasts ordered oldest to newest with a small gap between them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
toast_stack(content: impl Into<Element<'a, M>>, toasts: impl IntoIterator<Item = Toast<M>>)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBStacked notifications\fR: any number of toasts shown at once, in one column at the position of the first (\fB[toasts] position\fR by default), \fBtoasts\fR ordered oldest to newest with a small gap between them. At a bottom position the newest sits nearest the edge, and each toast has its own entrance, call to action and dismiss. The app owns the list (add, dismiss, cap its length); an empty iterator shows nothing and keeps \fBcontent\fR's place in the tree.
